    <string name="how_to_play">How to play</string>
    <string name="paranoia_description_1">The host starts as the \'answerer\' and the player to their right is the \'partner in crime\'. A question is shown only to them. They may discuss it, but the answerer gives the final answer. The chosen person must be someone from the group.</string>
    <string name="reveal_round">Reveal round</string>
    <string name="paranoia_description_2">After revealing the name, press \'Reveal your fate\'. A coin flip decides whether the question is revealed. If yes, the answerer shares it. If not, it stays secret. Then pass the device left and continue.</string>
    <string name="add_some_spice">Add some spice</string>
    <string name="paranoia_description_3">When answering, be vague or misleading. Hint around the question instead of being direct. This keeps others guessing and increases the paranoia.</string>
    <string name="why_paranoia">Why paranoia?</string>
    <string name="paranoia_description_4">The mix of questions makes players overthink everything. Do they like me? Hate me? Think I\'m weird or funny? That\'s what creates the paranoia.</string>
